================================================================================
 VERIFY closed-form pairwise overlap o(p,q) against EXACT  (p,q <= 16)
================================================================================
  tested 120 pairs, mismatches = 0
  spot: o(1,13)= 1/91  o(1,12)= 1/84  o(12,13)= 23/1092  o(5,9)= 1/63

================================================================================
 SYMBOLIC ASSEMBLY of cap_11 (j=2) and cap_10 (j=3) from closed forms
================================================================================
 j=2 (k=11): cap = 1 - 2/7 + o(1,13) = 1 - 2/7 + 1/91 = 66/91 = C(12,2)/91 = 66/91  OK
 j=3 (k=10): O2 = o(1,12)+o(1,13)+o(12,13) = 1/84+1/91+23/1092 = 4/91
            triple o(1,12,13) = 1/91  (= 1/(7*13) = narrowest nested arc inside I_0)
            cap = 1 - 3/7 + 4/91 - 1/91 = 55/91 = C(11,2)/91 = 55/91  OK -- cap_10 PROVED symbolically

================================================================================
 THE APEX-14 THRESHOLD in the overlap formula
================================================================================
 o(p,q) = 1/(7 max) + (offset terms that switch ON iff p+q > 14).  For the minimizer top pairs:
   o(1,13) = 1/(7*13) + 0   [p+q=14 <=14: offset OFF]
   o(1,12) = 1/(7*12) + 0   [p+q=13 <=14: offset OFF]
   o(12,13) = 1/(7*13) + 11/1092   [p+q=25 > 14: offset ON]
   o(11,13) = 1/(7*13) + 10/1001   [p+q=24 > 14: offset ON]
   o(11,12) = 1/(7*12) + 3/308   [p+q=23 > 14: offset ON]
